# Git commit identity

There is exactly one commit author: the repository git user (`git config user.name` / `user.email`).

- Do not add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `cursoragent@cursor.com`, or any Cursor/agent trailer to the commit message.
- Do not pass `git commit --author`.
- Do not set `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME`, `GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL`, `GIT_COMMITTER_NAME`, or `GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL` for commits.
- Write the message with a HEREDOC only. The `commit-msg` hook strips leftover Cursor trailers if the IDE injects them.

```bash
# ❌ BAD
git commit --author="Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>" -m "feat: x"

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# ✅ GOOD
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
feat: x

EOF
)"
```

IDE agents: turn off Cursor Settings → Agent → Attribution so the UI does not append a Cursor trailer.
